     "text": "```python\nfrom pedantic import count_calls, trace\nimport secrets\n\ndef find_majority_element(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the majority element of an array if it exists.\n    A majority element is an element that appears more than n//2 times in the array.\n    If no such element exists, returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Using the 'secrets' module for secure random selection, though not strictly necessary here.\n    # This is a best practice for handling sensitive operations, even if not directly applicable.\n    # The 'count_calls' decorator is used to track how often this function is called.\n    # The 'trace' decorator is used to provide debugging information.\n    @count_calls\n    @trace\n    def majority_element_helper(arr):\n        if not arr:\n            return None\n        # Using Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm for O(1) space complexity\n        candidate = None\n        count = 0\n        for num in arr:\n            if count == 0:\n                candidate = num\n            count += 1 if num == candidate else -1\n        # Verify if the candidate is actually the majority element\n        if arr.count(candidate) > len(arr) // 2:\n            return candidate\n        return None\n\n    return majority_element_helper(arr)\n```",
